exports[`legal text with Share v2 off > reads as before > children 1`] = `
"Children’s Privacy Notice
How Cleffy LLC treats information about children under 13, and how teachers can use Cleffy with younger students.
Who we are
DRAFT — awaiting legal review. Not in effect.
Cleffy is run by Cleffy LLC, a New York limited liability company, 245 East 37th Street, Apt 3E, New York, NY 10016, USA. You can reach us at privacy@cleffy.io about children’s privacy, or at support@cleffy.io for anything else.
Phone number — Max to supply
Children under 13 don’t have Cleffy accounts
Anyone who creates an account themselves, or joins a shared score as a guest through a share link, first answers an age check. If they do not meet the minimum age where they live (13, or older in some countries), no account is created.
A teacher who creates a student account confirms that the student meets the minimum age for the student’s country.
Using Cleffy with a young student on the teacher’s own screen
A teacher may use Cleffy in lessons with a student under the minimum age by showing a score on the teacher’s own device. The student does not sign in or type anything, and Cleffy collects nothing from the student.
How long we keep information
Because children under 13 do not have accounts, Cleffy does not hold their information. If we learn that we hold some anyway, we delete it. How long we keep everyone else’s information is set out in our Privacy Policy.
Parents
If you are a parent or guardian and think your child under 13 has given us information, write to privacy@cleffy.io. We delete anything we learn was collected from a child under 13.
Status of this notice
This notice is a draft. It is not in effect until counsel has reviewed it.
Counsel to confirm the internal-operations basis (16 CFR 312.5(c)(7)) and the notice contents (312.4(d))."
`;

